EXCLUDED: BRAND ASSETS

The ENS marks are not licensed under AGPL-3.0-only or MIT, whatever directory
they sit in: the ENS logo and wordmark, the ENS mark, and the ENS token icons,
as artwork. That means the SVG path data that draws a mark and any raster
export of it, wherever it appears, including inside a source file that one of
the licenses above otherwise covers.

Only the artwork is excluded. The code around it keeps the license for its
directory, so a component that renders a mark is AGPL-3.0-only or MIT like any
other file and you may copy and modify it. Replace the artwork with your own.

TRADEMARK.md lists where the marks currently live and sets out what you may and
may not do with them. Trademark rights are separate from the licenses above and
are not granted by them (AGPL-3.0 section 7(e)).

EXCLUDED: FONTS

No font file in this repository is licensed under AGPL-3.0-only or MIT,
whatever directory it is in. This applies to every .woff, .woff2, .ttf, .otf
and .eot file, including ones added after this notice was written. Each font
remains under its owner's own license.

  Geist, Geist Mono
      Owner:    Vercel (https://vercel.com/font)
      License:  SIL Open Font License 1.1, see the LICENSE-OFL.txt beside
                the files. Used by the Open Graph image renderer.
      Files:    apps/manager/public/og/fonts/
                apps/portal/src/assets/fonts/og/

The ABC Monument Grotesk family and ABC Marist (Dinamo Typefaces,
https://abcdinamo.com) are not in this repository. The apps load them at
runtime from https://fonts.ens.dev, which serves them only for ENS Labs' own
deployments, listed under "Official deployments" in TRADEMARK.md. Anywhere
else, including a fork, the CSS falls back to the generic family.

If you build or deploy anything from this repository and want the Dinamo
typefaces, you are responsible for licensing them and for pointing
apps/*/src/styles/fonts.css at your own copies rather than at fonts.ens.dev.
